Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ================================================================
; VMware Win7 Printer Fix - Legacy Printers Shell Folder
; ================================================================
;
; ISSUE:
; Windows 7 VM is running under VMware Workstation Player 16.2.5
; with VMware Tools 11.3.5.
; The host has multiple network printers installed.
; VMware successfully redirects all of them through the TPVM port,
; but Windows 7 Devices and Printers only displays the host`s
; default printer as a single printer object.
;
; The other redirected printers can be seen through the VMware
; printer properties, but Windows 7 does not display them as
; separate printer objects in the normal Devices and Printers
; interface.
;
; IMPORTANT:
; This has annoyed me and plagued my existence.
; This is NOT an RDP printer-redirection problem.
; RDP printer redirection Group Policy settings are not involved.
; VMware virtual printing is already enabled.
; The TPVM port is working.
; Do NOT delete the TPVM port or reinstall VMware Tools just
; because the printers appear grouped.
;
; FIX:
; This registry key restores the legacy Windows Printers
; shell folder. It provides an alternative/legacy printer
; namespace that can expose redirected VMware/ThinPrint printers
; individually instead of relying on the Windows 7 Devices and
; Printers view.
;
; DATE ADDED:
; 2026-09-16

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\Desktop\NameSpace\{2227a280-3aea-1069-a2de-08002b30309d}]
@="Printers"
